From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Thief: geometry given unchanged kept in the frames' buffers, and given again without its data

The game gives its whole world as dynamic geometry every frame: at the
Reflections in Red castle 6900 primitives, 650k vertices, every one of them
copied into the scene's storage and again into the frame's GPU buffer, its
textures found by name, its geometry info made anew -- about 4 ms a frame.

A primitive given with RT_PRIMITIVE_UNCHANGED (1u << 29) now keeps its
vertices, indices and texture coordinates in an arena: the first part of
each frame's dynamic buffers, the same place in all of them, written into a
frame's buffers once and not copied again while it comes unchanged (the
frame's other dynamic data follows the arena). And rgThiefRepeatPrimitives
gives such a primitive again as it was last given, without its data: its
geometry as it was, its textures found again only when the materials have
changed. RTGL1_METAL_NO_ARENA=1 turns it off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0137FfF2kXgpYFjmGxKqakLV
